>>
Rule 1 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 3 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 5 (index tensor (v_2) should be within the range of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, i) - 1
